<title>USA: U.S. M-2 money supply up $200 mln in June 2 week.</title>
<headline>U.S. M-2 money supply up $200 mln in June 2 week.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. M-2 money supply rose $200 million in the June 2 week to $3,910.6 billion, the Federal Reserve said.</p>
<p>The broader M-3 measure rose $7.8 billion to $5,069.6 billion. M-1 was up $6.9 billion to $1,071.8 billion, the Fed said.</p>
<p>The Fed said the four-week moving average of M-2 was $3,930.5 billion versus $3,899.4 billion in the previous week.</p>
<p>(( -- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660 ))</p>
